WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.970
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.650
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.160
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.500
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.240
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.580
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.650
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.630
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.270
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.170
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:32.520
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.260
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.990
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.800
The Blade Children must not be
allowed to exist in this world.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.700
Their existence is cursed
and should be detested.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.470
They must be exterminated.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.870
We cannot afford to sacrifice any more.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.040
Do you intend to seek out
the light of illusion

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.030
and continue wandering, Eyes?

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.050
Do you intend to leave me behind?

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.220
You've lost sight of reality

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.490
because you so earnestly
seek redemption.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.220
<i>Ayumu-kun won't be able to save us.</i>

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.490
The only ones who can save us...

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.490
...are ourselves.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.860
Kanone.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.400
The path you speak of
is enshrouded in darkness.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:32.560
I want to believe in Kiyotaka's
"happiness of those who believe"...

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.980
Very well. Then I have no choice.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.980
This is the end.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.110
I'll show you reality.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.520
Go to the underground
sewage utility tunnel.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.320
There you will find
the Blade Children's "Hell."

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.820
"The Mask's Confession"
There you will find
the Blade Children's "Hell."

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.310
"The Mask's Confession"

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.250
<i>So the target's expecting us...</i>

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:12.400
<i>Kanone guessed right.</i>

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.530
<i>Now to see if we can
pull this off or not...</i>

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.710
How about catching the Hunters

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.750
and getting information about
the police insider from them?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.820
That might be a good way to
learn about the situation.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.520
The question is how to get them...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.120
Hello, Bla-Chil!

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.290
Having a strategy meeting?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.460
Kanone?!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.980
<i>Kanone-kun! How did
you know we were here?</i>

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.860
Listen.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.970
Up until now, you've only
stayed on the defensive

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.000
whenever the Hunters drew you out.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.770
But now it's our turn to fight back.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.240
Don't the Hunters know
about the underground too?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.540
Yes, they do.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.980
But our meeting will be
entirely above ground.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.380
What would you do, Kosuke?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.450
I'd probably set traps
above ground to catch us,

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.660
and use the underground as
an emergency escape route.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.360
So we force them down there?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:12.830
We avoid the traps and
drive the enemy underground...

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.230
...where Eyes and I will
be waiting for them.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.400
A pincer attack, huh?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.080
Ryoko. See anything?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.170
No signs of snipers.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.420
There aren't even any
police officers around,

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.390
despite everything that happened here.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.090
It would seem we're right
in thinking there's a Hunter

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.020
on the police force...

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.510
Rio, how are things on your end?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.660
I've found the 12th one.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.470
They're all set in places
to prevent escape...

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.240
Lure us in, and then
keep us here with traps...

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.970
This is their style,
no doubt about it...

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.910
<i>We're making all the preparatory
moves this time, though.</i>

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.720
Everything's gone
according to plan so far.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.920
It's time for me to meet the target.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.920
Kosuke, don't do anything stupid.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:14.320
Our goal is to catch 'em
and get information.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.420
I know.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.740
You two move into position.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.180
Roger.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.450
<i>Rutherford. Kanone.</i>

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.680
<i>I'm counting on you to catch them.</i>

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.360
Senior Superintendent Kanzaka, was it?

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:00.070
I'm honored that you know
who I am, Kosuke Asazuki.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:02.570
With a Hunter in the
high ranks of the police,

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.070
it's only natural they would
do things extravagantly.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.840
I would say we both do
things extravagantly.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:20.650
Sorry, but you'll be the first to go.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.120
Give it up, Kanzaka!

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:32.070
There might've been mines buried there,

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.590
but you can't use the
same old tricks on us.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.940
Electronic jamming...

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:38.940
While we were at it,

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:42.500
we found the traps you
had all over the place.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.220
It would seem I've
been rather pre-empted.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:49.490
We want information from you.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:51.450
That's our only goal.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.920
And if I refuse to talk?

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.760
You'll talk.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.790
All we want is to
change this situation.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.260
Things will not go
as easily as you wanted...

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.490
He escaped underground,
just like we wanted.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.460
<i>Little does he know that
Eyes-kun and Kanone-kun</i>

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.730
are waiting for him.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.820
-Let's go after him!
-Yeah!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.490
I'm not home right now.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:03.150
Please leave your name
and message after the beep.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.400
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.370
I'm not calling for
any specific reason.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:15.740
It just seems too quiet,
and I can't see the sky...

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:22.440
I'm...worried about
the Blade Children.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.670
<i>Narumi-san, why won't you pick up...</i>

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.590
Where did he disappear to?

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.490
Did he really come this way?

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:37.930
I'm certain of it.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.400
<i>It's exactly like
Kanone-kun's blueprints.</i>

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.470
<i>Where...</i>

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.760
...are we?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.430
My guess is a gathering pipe
where all the rain water

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.430
drains into the sewers.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.120
I don't remember
Kanone mentioning that...

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.400
And that bomb just now...

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.740
Rutherford and Kanone
would be the last ones

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.100
to make a mistake...

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:26.380
It might be best to
consider our plan defeated.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.140
Let's just go.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.080
-This smell...
-Gasoline!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.480
Run!

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:49.800
Rio, Kosuke, Ryoko,
and one other person...

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.770
A Hunter...

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.200
There!

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.290
Even if we go up this,
there's no telling

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.620
if we'll make it back to the
first utility tunnel or not...

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:18.190
But there's no turning back now.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.930
From the way it was burning,

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.160
we'll eventually run out of oxygen...

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.400
Let's go!

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.970
What would be the most
effective place for a trap?

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:45.450
What is this place?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.080
My life has been horrible
ever since you got involved.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.680
You butt in on things by yourself,

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.210
which keeps me from doing anything!

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:14.020
You have become lost...

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:16.190
I must take you away.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.720
You're the one who's making me suffer!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.220
Stop getting in my way!

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:24.830
But you're nothing more
than a helpless child.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.230
<i>You'll never be Kiyotaka-san!</i>

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.020
First fire, and now water?!

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.600
Damn!

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:06.270
We need to stop the
water from coming out...

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.800
Looks like it's coming
from multiple places.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.740
I doubt the three of us
could block them all.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:14.210
Then there's nothing we can do...

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.610
Did that Kanaka bastard know what moves

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.140
we were going to make?

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.980
<i>What about Eyes-kun and Kanone-kun?</i>

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:29.160
What would Little Narumi
do at a time like this?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.960
Heh.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.830
Let's get ourselves out
of this and catch Kanzaka

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.000
before he laughs at us!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.900
-Agreed.
-Yeah!

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:46.710
A map of the switch yard area
and underground blueprints...

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:48.810
You can compare the two, right?

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.250
From the sound of your voice,
you seem to be in a hurry.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.080
Yeah.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.720
I'll contact you the instant I'm done!

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.710
Thanks.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.260
Oh!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.630
What is it, Rio?

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.000
What do you think this place is for?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.670
What do you mean?

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.270
I really doubt this place was made

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.810
just to catch us.

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:25.910
They're probably using
an abandoned facility,

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:27.750
like that one hotel.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:32.490
Yeah. It's obvious the water
is collected for something,

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.620
but what about it?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.060
If so, then wouldn't we be
inside a different building

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:40.160
and not part of the
utility tunnel anymore?

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.460
Maybe it's a water tank for experiments

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.570
or waste treatment.

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:47.400
<i>So if there were a door, then...</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.240
The lights are too bright
to really tell,

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.710
but it'd be on the ceiling.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.910
If we can just find the door

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.580
before the water reaches the top!

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:01.050
We're more likely to drown before then.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.850
How long can our bodies stand
this water temperature anyway?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.810
Rio!

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.870
You okay?! Hold on tight!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:33.880
Thanks!

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.960
<i>Narumi-san. I'm all set.</i>

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.120
That was fast.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.130
The path beneath that switch yard area

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.800
connects to a scientific
factory whose parent company

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:51.130
went bankrupt last month and the sewers.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:52.300
The sewers?

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.740
Yes. There are thick pipes protruding

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.000
from the abandoned
water treatment plant.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.750
Listen. When it's time to give up...

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.490
<i>Ryoko-chan...</i>

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.990
I won't give up yet!

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:17.220
I'll make sure you two live...

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.600
<i>-Eyes-kun?!
-Grab on!</i>

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.750
Is any of that useful to you?

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.620
Very. Sorry to bother you so suddenly.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.220
Oh, not at all.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.920
<i>Narumi-san. You're going, aren't you...</i>

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.120
The sky...

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.490
The stars are out now.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.500
You're right...

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.760
Be careful.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.480
We owe you one, Rutherford!

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.710
You did well to know we were here.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.550
Yes...

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.180
Thanks, Rutherford.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.240
That was way too close...

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.380
Rio?!

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.460
Can you stand?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.930
Yes...

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.230
<i>Thanks, Eyes-kun.</i>

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.000
It's him!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:54.090
Even if you stand up
and take a step forward,

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.790
there is no place in this world for you.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.900
Even so, we'll still
stand up and walk ahead.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.230
No matter what our fate may be.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:13.640
Cursed children...

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.910
Despair awaits you ahead.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.710
Only death and destruction remain

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:21.920
on the path you have trampled.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.620
Wait! Hear us out!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:26.660
If you're going to pray for sleep,

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.490
then I'll be glad to listen.

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.650
Enough with the
high-and-mighty talk, Hunter!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.110
There's no escape.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:50.700
You're going to tell us
everything about you guys.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.780
This is the first time

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:58.690
I have ever looked up
at you Blade Children.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.720
Though I have looked down upon you

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.230
and prayed for your eternal rest.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:06.560
Return to the darkness
that which was born from it.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.300
That is our duty.

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:12.570
Your duty? What are you, Death?!

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.540
<i>You're Death.</i>

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.180
Hear us out!

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.740
All we want is to
change this situation!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:38.260
Don't move!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.920
<i>-Ryoko!
-Ryoko-chan!</i>

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.900
Stay back or I snap her neck.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.130
Let go!

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.030
Ryoko!

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.310
<i>I won't let you die!</i>

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:14.100
-Hold on!
-Don't let go!

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:18.400
Are you honestly attempting to save me?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:21.240
You have no salvation.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:26.410
You haven't the capacity to save
others, much less yourselves.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.480
As you can see...

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.050
Stop! You'll fall!

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:33.150
My life doesn't matter.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:37.320
Even if we cease to be,
you'll still be cursed.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.750
Kanone Hilbert realized this fact.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.060
Kanone?!

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:43.260
<i>Eyes-kun!</i>

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.460
Eyes Rutherford.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:47.990
I take it you've already heard?

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:53.340
It was Kanone Hilbert who deceived you.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:56.200
He was our collaborator.

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:04.570
That can't be...

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.350
Blade Children...

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.520
Cursed children...

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.090
No!

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:20.730
Return to the darkness

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:22.560
with your odious fate...

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.400
No!

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.450
Ayumu Narumi...

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.080
Tell me...

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:53.990
Why were we born?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.090
Tell me...

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:02.430
Why are we alive?

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:11.080
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:17.780
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:35.930
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:41.570
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:47.480
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:54.050
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:59.790
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:05.000
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:10.840
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:22.450
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:28.220
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:34.520
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:40.750
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:44.690
When it rains, it pours!

00:22:44.690 --> 00:22:46.460
There are premonitions
of spring showers...

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:49.460
Why exactly does the
sky shed its tears?!

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:51.500
<i>Next episode's highlight is
when Detective Hiyono-chan</i>

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:54.630
checks to see if a piece of
happiness really does escape

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:57.100
each time you sigh!

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:59.600
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:00.940
Relentless Rain

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:02.640
Every night has a morning,

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:04.610
so these rainy days won't last forever!

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:06.700
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
